# Owner brief — repo clean-up and organisation (19 Oct 2026, verbatim)

OK I think the current version of the segment filter is good enough I dont want to look at it any more.

Plan and execute a clean up, and organization of the repo, I want:

(1) clear distinction of the following aspects of the repo:

(A) development of OCR, and our Segmenter: (i) the slow one (ii) the next gen (iii) the one built on top of small detector
(B) creation of training data for OCR:
(a) running google OCR on pages
(b) tools built on top of (A)'s segmenter and so on (the ones we are working on now) for correcting and filtering these
(c) the exact pipeline this process takes, which should organize the whole work of (B)
(d) the revision pipeline for (B.b) including the artifacts and how we publish for human review

I want you to create comprehensive documentation for these, an AGENTS md that explains our process (as described above) and a README. And generally removing what is not required.
Your process hsould involve either doing this in a new branch, or whatever other method allows easy comparison for an xhigh astra reviewer at the end given my brief.

FILE docs/cleanup_20261019/PLAN.md
# Clean-up plan — greek-ocr-toolkit, 19 Oct 2026

Owner brief: `OWNER_BRIEF.md` (verbatim). Inventory: `inventory/` (CLEAN1A code, CLEAN1B docs/size, CLEAN1C branches). Every phase is a Sol run; the coordinator writes briefs and reviews; the owner gates push/merge to `main`.

## End state
One `main` that holds everything good, organised by the owner's taxonomy, with the clean-up reviewable as one change (xhigh Astra review against the brief). Old branches stay as history until the owner says otherwise. Nothing is removed from git history.

## Taxonomy → repository

| Slot | Meaning (owner) | Code (unchanged import paths) | Documentation home |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | development of OCR and our segmenter | `greekocr/{synth,warmstart,score,real,recogniser}` + segmenters below | `docs/A_ocr_development/` |
| A.i | the slow segmenter | `greekocr/pages` (pixel-first page lines; crop primitives in `greekocr/glyphs`) | `docs/A_ocr_development/segmenters/SLOW_PIXEL.md` |
| A.ii | the next-generation segmenter | `prototypes/fast_lines/stack` at R8 (astra/ff-merged) | `docs/A_ocr_development/segmenters/NEXT_GEN_R8.md` |
| A.iii | the one built on top of the small detector | same stack at R7: PaddleOCR PP-OCRv6 small + heuristics (`shared.detector.Detector`, `layout_barriers.fast`) | `docs/A_ocr_development/segmenters/SMALL_DETECTOR_R7.md` + `MODEL_GENERATIONS.md` |
| B | creation of training data for OCR | `greekocr/harvest`, `greekocr/readers`, `greekocr/labelfix`, `greekocr/numerics`, `scripts/{harvest,labelfix,secondary,numerics}` | `docs/B_training_data/` |
| B.a | running Google OCR on pages | `greekocr/readers/services/{google_docai,docai_manifest,docai_driver}`, `harvest/page_reads`, source collectors | `docs/B_training_data/a_google_ocr/` |
| B.b | correcting and filtering tools on top of the segmenter | sf7 polytonic (`labelfix`), RU1 Cyrillic + N1 numerics + dashes (`scripts/secondary`, `greekocr/numerics`), segmentation filter 0.9-s4 + content gate 0.3 (`harvest/{geometry_observations,row_inclusion,neighbour_words,orientation_screen,numeric_cells,filtering_assets}`, Rust `scripts/harvest/filter_runtime`) | `docs/B_training_data/b_tools/` (one doc per tool, versioned) |
| B.c | the exact pipeline that organises B | `greekocr/harvest/line_pipeline*.py`; `pipeline.mmd` + README (pipeline 0.3) | `docs/B_training_data/c_pipeline/` (the organising document of B) |
| B.d | the revision pipeline for B.b, artifacts, human review | `greekocr/adjudicate` (owner sheet package), `labelfix/sheet.py` | `docs/B_training_data/d_review/` (HUMAN_REVIEW_SHEETS.md + publishing protocol) |
| shared | deploy, ops, verify, types, cli, vendor, Clariden scripts | unchanged | `docs/shared/` |
| records | completed briefs, reports, hand-offs, receipts | — | `docs/records/<track>/` (RECORD status; nothing rewritten) |

Open mapping for the owner: A.ii/A.iii are two generations of one fast stack (gen 2 = small Paddle + heuristics, gen 3 = R8 revision). Proposed: A.ii = R8 (current), A.iii = R7 small-detector lineage (record). `greekocr/lines`, `scripts/lines`, `docs/lines` are empty and go.

## Data policy (the main removal)
Tracked data files dominate the repo: jsonl pools, census exports, keys, bundles of 90–477 MB each, 4.8–7 GB of tracked docs per branch, .git 3.6 GB. Rule after the clean-up: no tracked file over 5 MB; bulk artifacts (crops, pools, census exports, keys, bundles, HTML sheets, montages, pytest XML) live under an external data root with a receipt (path, bytes, sha256, producing commit) kept in `docs/records/`; `.gitignore` patterns + a size-guard test. History is not rewritten (the owner decides later whether to shrink `.git`).

## Phases (Sol runs; parallel where independent)
| Phase | Run(s) | Content | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | CLEAN1A/B/C (done) | inventories | — |
| 2 | CLEAN2 (one run, sequential merges) | assemble `cleanup/20261019` = sol/recut-v1 + fable (contained) + sol/collect-v3 + sol/source-inventory + opus/spellcheck + opus/secondary-corrections + opus/seg-census + coord/review-sheets + opus/sol-reading + astra/ff-merged + the two origin/main README commits; conflict rules for `greekocr/labelfix/text.py`, `pyproject.toml`, `.gitignore`, `docs/INVENTORY.md`; commit the authoritative uncommitted work (Rust runtime, recut edits) per the leads' answers; full test suite green | leads' answers on dirty worktrees |
| 3 | CLEAN3 | data out of git: list every tracked file > 5 MB and every bulk artifact directory; move to the data root with receipts; `git rm --cached`; ignore patterns; size-guard test | coordinator approves the path list before any move (owner rule: inspected path lists) |
| 4 | CLEAN4 | layout: `docs/` into A / B / shared / records; remove empties, generated trees, superseded docs; fix version drift (pipeline docs 0.5 → 0.9-s4 + gate 0.3) | — |
| 5 | CLEAN5A–E in parallel | documentation: 5A segmenters (A.i–iii + generations), 5B B.a + B.c (Google OCR on pages; the pipeline as the organising doc), 5C B.b tools (one doc per tool with version, inputs, outputs, evidence), 5D B.d review pipeline (sheets, artifacts, publishing, marks), 5E README + AGENTS.md from the coordinator's outline | coordinator review of each |
| 6 | ASTRA xhigh | review against `OWNER_BRIEF.md`: base = `cleanup/20261019` at the end of phase 2 (integration only), head = after phase 5; ≤ 2 fix cycles | owner go to merge to `main` |

