# CLEAN1C — branch summary

Measured 56 local branches and 45 worktree registrations: **26 dirty, 18 clean, one unavailable**; 23 remain dirty after ignoring environments/caches. Full names and classifications are in [branches.json](branches.json), with ancestry and exact shared-path stats in [INVENTORY_BRANCHES.md](INVENTORY_BRANCHES.md).

Uncommitted work matters: **B(b)/B(c), recut** has tracked edits to `geometry_observations.py`, `row_inclusion.py` and `pyproject.toml`, plus untracked pipeline/runtime/review files. **B(a)/B(c), source-inventory** has **1,825 tracked deletions**, one modification and 3,492 untracked source/doc files; intent is unknown. **A(ii)/A(iii), ff-plan** has seven tracked planning edits. Collector and scanner worktrees have tracked report/test edits; secondary corrections and many correction/R2 worktrees have untracked source or review artifacts. Three dirty worktrees contain only ignored environment entries. The unavailable detached registration is already marked prunable; it was not changed.

The 10 **INTEGRATE candidates** preserve A development (`astra/ff-merged`), B(a) acquisition/provenance (`sol/collect-v3`, `sol/source-inventory`), B(b) tools (`fable/label-correction`, `sol/recut-v1`, `opus/spellcheck`, `opus/secondary-corrections`), B(c) pipeline (`opus/seg-census`), and B(d) review/scanner (`coord/review-sheets`, `opus/sol-reading`). Account for fable first: its exact tip precedes recut, spellcheck, secondary, seg-census and review-sheets. The other candidate tips are divergent; **no total merge order is established**. Functional review order is provenance/collector → recut/crop identity → corrective result contracts → frozen pipeline → review consumers; this is an inference, not commit ancestry. INTEGRATE does not require merging all historical artifacts.

All 45 candidate pairs were checked. Paths changed on both sides with different head contents are **`greekocr/labelfix/text.py`** across correction versus recut/pipeline heads; **`pyproject.toml`** for review-sheets/seg-census; **`.gitignore`** for scanner/collector versus recut; and **`docs/INVENTORY.md`** for fast-lines versus every later-main candidate. Other apparent head differences are inherited/unilateral. Actual textual merge conflicts are unknown: no merge was attempted.

Coordinator decisions: identify authoritative recut working files; explain source-inventory deletions; preserve dirty planner/scanner work; decide adoption of the 11 UNSURE survey/mask/Wikisource/R2/experiment heads; reconcile older script allowances with the owner's frozen gate. Recorded remote refs are unfetched: main is 53 ahead/2 behind origin/main; live remote state is unknown. All 56 local heads rechecked unchanged. No tests, project scripts, network, commits or layout recommendations.

docs/cleanup_20261019/inventory/INVENTORY_BRANCHES.md:1:# CLEAN1C — local branches and worktrees
docs/cleanup_20261019/inventory/INVENTORY_BRANCHES.md:5:## Scope, definitions and limits
docs/cleanup_20261019/inventory/INVENTORY_BRANCHES.md:11:**Owner classification:** A(i) slow OCR/segmenter; A(ii) next-generation development; A(iii) segmenter built on the small detector; B(a) page acquisition/Google Document AI; B(b) correction/filtering tools; B(c) exact organising pipeline; B(d) revision artifacts/sheets and human-review publication; shared infrastructure; obsolete; unsure. Multiple classifications are allowed. The fast-line documentation says the small-detector and current-revision work share `prototypes/fast_lines/stack`; therefore A(ii)/A(iii) are jointly tagged rather than inventing a third installed tree. The slow package is `greekocr/pages`.
docs/cleanup_20261019/inventory/INVENTORY_BRANCHES.md:13:**Status is an editorial inventory judgement, separate from classification.** INTEGRATE means the branch's current code/docs/provenance must be accounted for in a cleanup comparison, not that every historical artifact should be merged. CLOSED means contained support work or an explicitly closed/stopped/superseded track; it does not mean obsolete, accepted, or safe to delete. UNSURE preserves unresolved adoption decisions. ACTIVE is the baseline/current coordination branch. STALE marks the older public README. Counts: 10 INTEGRATE, 32 CLOSED, 11 UNSURE, 2 ACTIVE, 1 STALE.
