Clariden has three measured job kinds: **regression**, **parity**, and **census** (filter + correction import + composition/admission/dedup/export). Imported corrections are not separate reader jobs. `filter_worker.sbatch` is the earlier thin adapter with inventory/prepare/qualify/census/census-preflight modes; archived census04 separates the three bounded jobs. Follow the [runbook](RUNBOOK_CLARIDEN.md) for their different defaults and verify→smoke→full boundaries.

## Tests and interpretation

`tests/test_line_pipeline.py` covers routing order, binding, composition/UTF-8 spans, scoped negatives/holds, codec/CTC, cohort aliases, restart/generation publication and crop dedup. `tests/test_seg_small.py`, `test_seg_curve.py` and `test_seg_deskew.py` cover the named geometry changes; the S4 receipt records 1,288 fresh replay rows with 966 non-small results byte-identical to S3. Historical census04 package verification records 292 tests + 13 subtests and 150+888 verdict/reason parity for **its 0.8 build**. SEG10 reruns the specified seven test files offline: **248 passed in 4.21s**, zero failures; see the adoption report for the temporary layout compatibility view and full logs. These bounded checks are not population accuracy claims. The frozen 888-row parity cannot qualify a changed policy simply by being repeated as a historical number.

