docs/B_training_data/README.md:12:The live [tool manifest](../harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json) identifies pipeline 0.3's component generations: segmentation 0.9-s4, content gate/final eligibility 0.3, polytonic 0.7, Cyrillic 0.3, numerics 0.2 and dashes 0.1. Segmentation is frozen as accepted; SF7 remains `candidate_pre_audit`, N1 is assisted, and dashes only tag. Historical deployed packages and their outcomes stay attached to their recorded versions. This layout does not adopt a candidate or establish a fresh population result.
docs/A_ocr_development/MODEL_GENERATIONS.md:70:Thus the 12 October source-equality sentence is updated, not copied as a current fact. The old algorithm document's document-over-code rule is also historical; current code and the authoritative B manifest win for this integration. B segmentation `0.9-s4` / gate `0.3` are crop-policy versions in `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json`, not generation 3 or R8 detector releases.
docs/A_ocr_development/README.md:15:The shared primitives do not collapse these scopes. `greekocr/glyphs/components.py` is crop geometry used by A and B; the B segmentation **filter** is not one of A's three page segmenter generations. The authoritative B manifest, `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json`, names segmentation `0.9-s4`, content gate `0.3`, polytonic `0.7`, Cyrillic `0.3`, numerics `0.2`, and dashes `0.1`. These are named tool generations, not R7/R8 or neural-model versions. B's owner-accepted segmentation state is `accepted_as_is`; this A documentation grants no tuning or pipeline work.
docs/B_training_data/d_review/PUBLISHING.md:37:| SEG final sheet, **local/unpublished** | `seg09:<line_id>` | `docs/records/harvest/seg_steps/sheet/seg09_sheet.html`: 279 unique cards, union of 238 changed lines and 59 proposal lines, overlap 18. Changed-set categories: 28 disagree, 77 newly agree, 133 unjudged. Compares 0.8 with 0.9-s4 using saved evidence; owner marks appear as historical text, never seeded. `receipt.json` says `published:false`; screenshot unavailable. No publication URL or later owner decision is claimed. |
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/CONTENT_GATE.md:94:Expected scripts require accurate provenance-bound declarations. A HOLD can be real apparatus, not OCR noise; raw script presence cannot settle printed glyph identity. The gate intentionally drops homoglyph words rather than guessing. Codec classification can make ordinals/micro signs appear foreign. Missing dimensions HOLD. Finite-set diagnostic eligibility omits the full production/correction context; it must not be presented as ADMIT counts. The gate re-report's .30–1.95 fitted optimum is not a code change to segmentation's .50–1.50 defaults.
docs/B_training_data/d_review/README.md:3:Documentation for `docs/B_training_data/d_review/`, read against the integrated cleanup branch on 19 October 2026. This directory describes review and evidence, not a pipeline execution. Current tool identities come from `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json`: segmentation **0.9-s4**, content gate **0.3**, polytonic **0.7** (SF7 `candidate_pre_audit`), Cyrillic **0.3**, numerics **0.2** (assisted; automatic candidate rejected), dashes **0.1** (tags only). Older handoffs describe their recorded generations; they do not override this manifest.
docs/B_training_data/d_review/README.md:52:S4's report deduplicates 240 explicit entries to 235 line IDs by latest timestamp, then file order. Agreement rises from 155/235 (0.8) to 189/235 (0.9-s4); the 135 rated calibration subset rises 94→109/135. The 150-line gate2 rubric gives FP/FN/UNC 18/14/11→16/15/0. These are different denominators and evidence types. The original SEGEVAL four-question scorer instead reports 29/50 false rejects and 5/100 misses; its rubric and sampled decision strata must stay attached to those figures. The early context pack's 0.8 FN=11 and the archived sheet builder's baseline headline are superseded by the specific saved scoring records, not copied into the current comparison.
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/README.md:9:| [SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md](SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md) | 0.9-s4 | Three-rule filter plus whole-body visibility, clockwise turns, curved measurement and small all-component boxes; frozen. Checked-in band .50–1.50; .30–2.00 is recorded proposal evidence. |
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/README.md:68:The requested .30–2.00 band is not wired into the checked-in segmentation service: code defaults remain .50–1.50. The d94cff curved short-side failure remains documented and unfixed. SF7 remains candidate_pre_audit. RU4/N1 lack LQB truth coverage of their released edits; this is not a clean independent benchmark win. LQB still has external peer-worktree imports and registry paths. Historical receipts retain original paths/hashes; cleanup must preserve retrievability with custody receipts before any approved relocation. This run touches none of those files.
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md:1:# Segmentation filter — 0.9-s4
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md:7:Authority is the checked-in implementation and `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json`. That manifest names **0.9-s4**. `docs/records/harvest/seg_steps/NOTES_FOR_LATER_STEPS.md` records the owner's freeze and no further segmentation steps.
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md:9:**Band discrepancy:** the requested history includes 0.30–2.00. `s5/BAND_PROPOSAL.md` explicitly calls that a proposal, not adoption. The actual `segmentation-policy.js` defaults remain lower=.5, upper=1.5; `service.mjs` calls both ordinary and small-crop length functions without overrides. Thus this branch implements **0.50–1.50**, not 0.30–2.00. The wider band and its gate-filtered re-report are documented below as evidence, not silently substituted into current behavior.
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md:35:| 0.9-s4 | Google visible characters ≤8 and crop long/short≤6: all extracted components define the box; row-only no-main abstention defers to length/padding. Others retain S3. |
docs/B_training_data/b_tools/SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md:54:The Rust streaming predictor `scripts/harvest/filter_runtime/src/main.rs` reads frozen JSON coefficients, selects the script model or pooled fallback, uses model index 2, evaluates `exp(clamp(sum([1, ln(long/short), 0] * coefficients), 0, 12)) - 1`, and never fits. Its Cargo package version **0.1.0** is separate from segmentation **0.9-s4**. Rule 2 compares `(characters+1)/(predicted+1)` inclusively with the checked-in **.5–1.5** interval. Rule 3 requires `(crop_height-upright_box_height)/row_frame_height ≤1.5`; small crops use their all-component height for both box height and denominator.
docs/B_training_data/c_pipeline/RUNBOOK_CLARIDEN.md:11:| Current top-level integrated source | `python -B -m greekocr.harvest.line_pipeline_census`; pipeline 0.3, segmentation **0.9-s4**, gate/final **0.3**, census 0.5 | Needs its own exact package/config/runtime/parity qualification. Historical census03/04 receipts do not establish this build's deployment or full result. |
docs/B_training_data/c_pipeline/README.md:28:**Band adoption provenance:** this is a coordinator decision under the owner's end-to-end mandate (“you don't have to wait for me, resolve these end to end”), recorded in the coordinator ledger on **19 October at 21:34**. It was reported to the owner in writing: “frozen the configuration at 0.9-s4 measurement, gate 0.3, band 0.30–2.00, one band for everything”. The task records no objection since. This provenance is supplied by the coordinator; it is **not an owner ruling**. The one inclusive 0.30–2.00 band applies to numeric/non-numeric and small/non-small rows, with mode 2, padding 1.5, the gate and S4 measurement unchanged. It was fitted on owner marks; this adoption is not an independent generalization result.
docs/B_training_data/c_pipeline/README.md:30:SEG10 ports the exact archived census03 hunks: `automatic_result()` uses `not re.search(r"\d\s*[.\-·]\s*\d", text)` for numeric candidate negatives, and `Ledger.deduplicate()` unions `final_policy.heldout_crop_sha256` into its existing held-out set. The deployed census04 package remains a separate historical 0.8 build; its results are not a current production census. Tool iterations move numerics 0.2→0.3 (the returned automatic result is bound to the numerics manifest entry) and census 0.5→0.6. Segmentation appends its thirteenth documented iteration, 0.9-s4→0.9-s5 (the existing suffix convention is eight base iterations plus five steps); pipeline 0.3→0.3.1 is a patch identifier. All other tool generation numbers remain unchanged; exact shared component hashes are regenerated.
