     1	# B.b — correcting and filtering tools built on the segmenter
     2	
     3	## Purpose
     4	
     5	Index the tools that turn sourced Google OCR labels and segmenter evidence into reviewable correction/filter decisions. This directory is **tool documentation**, maintained in `docs/B_training_data/b_tools/` under the taxonomy in `docs/cleanup_20261019/PLAN.md`. B.a supplies page OCR; B.c organizes the exact pipeline; B.d owns review artifacts and publication. Those interfaces do not make a proposed tool adopted or a single-stage KEEP training admission.
     6	
     7	| Document | Current identity | Scope / release boundary |
     8	| --- | --- | --- |
     9	| [SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md](SEGMENTATION_FILTER.md) | 0.9-s4 | Three-rule filter plus whole-body visibility, clockwise turns, curved measurement and small all-component boxes; frozen. Checked-in band .50–1.50; .30–2.00 is recorded proposal evidence. |
    10	| [CONTENT_GATE.md](CONTENT_GATE.md) | 0.3; final eligibility 0.3 | Mixed-word DROP, unexpected-script HOLD, raw short-line exclusion and aligned cell exemption. |
    11	| [POLYTONIC_SF7.md](POLYTONIC_SF7.md) | 0.7 /SF7 A | Mark correction candidate_pre_audit; full audit unresolved, no binding. |
    12	| [CYRILLIC_RU1.md](CYRILLIC_RU1.md) | 0.3 /ru1_v3_edits | Historical Russian final ь→ъ; sparse raw-parent train and test/dev versions. |
    13	| [NUMERICS_N1.md](NUMERICS_N1.md) | 0.2 /n1_v1_w1 | Assisted `-`/`.`→`·`; rejected automatic ink rule stays disabled. |
    14	| [DASHES.md](DASHES.md) | 0.1 | Literal dash tags, no general repair. |
    15	| [LABEL_QUALITY_BENCHMARK.md](LABEL_QUALITY_BENCHMARK.md) | Frozen truth_v1_1; scorer schema v1.2 | Per-class label comparison, exposure guards and version registry; not another corrector. |
    59	
    60	SF7's current audit is **70 correct /30 pending of100**, not a passed full audit. RU1's wave-1c effect is targeted (**1.68→1.25%** on 135 changed rows), with class-CER gate refuted. N1's **63 lead-confirmed edits** are assisted, while its automatic candidate failed **0/5**. LQB truth_v1_1 has **61,463 items**, but relevant release coverage/exposure still determines what can be measured. Details and exact limitations belong to the linked tool pages.
    61	
    62	## Tests
    63	
    64	these documents document existing test files and original receipts. **No pipeline, tests, readers, fitting, training or git writes were run for CLEAN5C.** Documentation verification consists of checking the eight files, common template, source paths, internal links, quoted rules and recorded numbers. Historical counts are labelled by run rather than presented as current all-green integration results.
    65	
    66	## Known limitations
    67	
    68	The requested .30–2.00 band is not wired into the checked-in segmentation service: code defaults remain .50–1.50. The d94cff curved short-side failure remains documented and unfixed. SF7 remains candidate_pre_audit. RU4/N1 lack LQB truth coverage of their released edits; this is not a clean independent benchmark win. LQB still has external peer-worktree imports and registry paths. Historical receipts retain original paths/hashes; cleanup must preserve retrievability with custody receipts before any approved relocation. This run touches none of those files.
    69	
    70	## Code paths
    71	
    72	Filters/integration: `greekocr/harvest/{line_pipeline.py,line_pipeline_native.py,filtering_assets/}` and `scripts/harvest/filter_runtime/`. Label correction/scoring: `greekocr/{labelfix,numerics}/`, `scripts/{labelfix,secondary,numerics,lqb}/`. Review: `greekocr/adjudicate/owner_sheet.py`; contract `docs/B_training_data/d_review/HUMAN_REVIEW_SHEETS.md`. Code paths remain unchanged by this documentation work.
    73	
    74	## Sources read
    75	
     1	# Segmentation filter — 0.9-s4
     2	
     3	## Purpose
     4	
     5	Screen an immutable Google-labelled crop for other rows, output length relative to measured ink, and vertical padding. A segmentation KEEP passes this screen; it does not certify the transcription or training admission. This is a B.b document for the documentation home `docs/B_training_data/b_tools/`, as mapped in `docs/cleanup_20261019/PLAN.md`.
     6	
     7	Authority is the checked-in implementation and `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json`. That manifest names **0.9-s4**. `docs/records/harvest/seg_steps/NOTES_FOR_LATER_STEPS.md` records the owner's freeze and no further segmentation steps.
     8	
     9	**Band discrepancy:** the requested history includes 0.30–2.00. `s5/BAND_PROPOSAL.md` explicitly calls that a proposal, not adoption. The actual `segmentation-policy.js` defaults remain lower=.5, upper=1.5; `service.mjs` calls both ordinary and small-crop length functions without overrides. Thus this branch implements **0.50–1.50**, not 0.30–2.00. The wider band and its gate-filtered re-report are documented below as evidence, not silently substituted into current behavior.
    10	
    11	## Owner rules it implements, quoted
    12	
    13	`docs/records/harvest/collect_v3_admission/segeval1/gate2/HANDOFF.md` quotes the owner:
    14	
    50	Rule 1 runs first. An additional complete row or >2 whole neighbour words drops. Missing main row or unresolved direction can abstain; S4 small-crop orchestration defers the no-main abstention while preserving positive neighbour DROPs. Stage B is skipped when the gate does not pass.
    51	
    52	For ordinary crops, main-row TEXT_ROLES ink defines the text box. S2 uses a de-skewed frame; S3 uses the existing base polyline's nearest feet, cumulative arc length s and signed normal n. It does not fit a new curve. Actual straight constructions use the original rotation arithmetic. The upright box remains the padding envelope. S4 small crops instead use the union of **every extracted component's axis-aligned bounds**, including marks, specks, rules and neighbour roles. Existing extraction already omits area<3 noise; S4 does not introduce a new noise filter. Width is passed as `long_side` and height as `short_side` for small crops, without sorting them; other crops use max/min frame extents.
    53	
    54	The Rust streaming predictor `scripts/harvest/filter_runtime/src/main.rs` reads frozen JSON coefficients, selects the script model or pooled fallback, uses model index 2, evaluates `exp(clamp(sum([1, ln(long/short), 0] * coefficients), 0, 12)) - 1`, and never fits. Its Cargo package version **0.1.0** is separate from segmentation **0.9-s4**. Rule 2 compares `(characters+1)/(predicted+1)` inclusively with the checked-in **.5–1.5** interval. Rule 3 requires `(crop_height-upright_box_height)/row_frame_height ≤1.5`; small crops use their all-component height for both box height and denominator.
    55	
    56	## Outputs and reason codes
    57	
    58	Native results carry tool version, row binding, raw-text SHA, verdict/reason, frame, measurements, warnings and detector/gate evidence. Verdicts are KEEP, DROP, UNCERTAIN; the pipeline handles uncertainty separately from a DROP.
