     2	
     3	# B — line-data pipeline 0.3
     4	
     5	This is the organising document for creation of OCR training data: **B.a** acquires pages and Google observations; **B.b** supplies segmentation, filtering and qualified correction evidence; **B.c** binds those inputs and makes auditable row decisions; **B.d** supplies owner review sheets and returned decisions. See [Google page reads](../../B_training_data/a_google_ocr/README.md), [sources and split custody](../../B_training_data/a_google_ocr/SOURCES.md), [the corrected graph](../../B_training_data/c_pipeline/pipeline.mmd) and [Clariden runbook](../../B_training_data/c_pipeline/RUNBOOK_CLARIDEN.md).
     6	
     7	Documentation for `cleanup/20261019`, inspected 19 October 2026. All source paths are repository-relative. This describes the **top-level implemented code**, with historical deployed bundles identified separately. Nothing was executed, trained, deployed or released by this documentation task.
     8	
     9	## Authority and version drift
    10	
    11	`greekocr/harvest/line_pipeline.py` declares `PIPELINE_VERSION = "0.3"`. `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json` supplies named tool generations and exact component hashes/digests. Versions count documented methods, not commits or measured accuracy.
    12	
    13	| Component | Current manifest version | Scope |
    14	|---|---|---|
    15	| Inventory | 0.1 | Raw text scripts, words, characters, marks, punctuation and counts |
    16	| Content gate | **0.3** | Mixed-script DROP, unexpected-script HOLD, raw-text length/cell rules before native work |
    17	| Segmentation | **0.9-s4** | Crop-only neighbour gate, clockwise tall-crop normalization, curved main-row measurement; all-component small-segment branch |
    18	| Polytonic | **0.7 / SF7** | Seven named generations; saved `candidate_pre_audit` release is proposal-only |
    19	| Cyrillic | **0.3 / RU1** | Historical Russian word-final `ь→ъ` only |
    20	| Numerics | **0.2 / N1** | Assisted separator corrections; rejected automatic candidate remains disabled |
    21	| Dashes | **0.1** | Tags only, no general repair release |
    22	| Content repair | 0.2 | Independent evidence bound to exact row/content/profile |
    23	| Composer | 0.2 | Compatible raw-parent spans, coverage and conflict checks |
    24	| Final eligibility | **0.3** | Cell exemption matches early gate; content/confidence/codec/CTC/split checks remain |
    25	| Census orchestration | **0.5** | Durable inventory, bounded parallel native execution, protected frozen-parent aliases |
    26	| Codec | **v2** | `greekocr/_vendor/codec/v2.json`, NFD atoms; SHA256 `94485f72eac0aaf2324dc60b1c02110b271d362a79c440e2ce6bf6f4604997b9` |
    27	
    28	The superseded pipeline README called segmentation 0.5 and census 0.3; its graph labelled pipeline 0.2 and segmentation 0.5. Those descriptions are retained only as dated records. This README and adjacent `pipeline.mmd` are corrected replacements; the superseded originals are preserved in `docs/records/harvest/line_pipeline_legacy/`. The JS policy file's “0.8” comment describes its unchanged three-rule functions; current native geometry and S4 orchestration in `crop-tools.py`, `line_pipeline_native.py` and `service.mjs` make the complete tool **0.9-s4**.
    29	
    30	There are two additional integration discrepancies. The archived census03 `integration_fixes.diff` adds (1) digit/separator/digit numeric-adjacency negatives and (2) union of `final_policy.heldout_crop_sha256` into deduplication. **Both are absent from the inspected top-level code.** `automatic_result()` still uses `not any(c in text for c in ".-·")`; `Ledger.deduplicate()` protects only registered dev/test crop hashes. The archived census04 package preserves the repaired census03 code, but is a separate 0.8 deployment. Neither its results nor its external-crop protection can be attributed to the current top-level build. This document records the discrepancy and changes no code.

