9:1. **Line id** (monospace), the **tool pill** (`tool: KEEP` / `DROP` / `UNCERTAIN`, the latest version's verdict) and the owner's **mark badge** (`✓ KEEP` / `✗ DROP`).
10:2. **The crop**, always with the **Google text directly beneath it** in the table (rule: crop and text are judged together). Display size: natural size up to 3×, never wider than the card (940 px) nor taller than 300 px. Hover or click gives a 3× lens; `z` shows the crop at 3× with sideways scrolling.
11:3. **Evidence overlays** drawn as SVG on the crop, scaled with it, toggled with `b`: blue = upright text box; magenta = de-skewed box; green = detected main row (ascender, base); orange dashed = other rows; red box = whole neighbour word; grey dashed = cut-off word; orange edge bar / red dot = cut diagnostics. Overlays are the tool's saved evidence, never recomputed in the page.
12:4. **Rows** (label + text): Google text; the tool's inventory/measurements in plain words ("MAIN: 52 letters, complete, covers 98% | ABOVE: 1% visible, 0 whole / 13 cut-off words"); **exactly the last two tool versions** ("0.7" and "0.8 (latest)"), each with verdict, reason and the numbers behind it; "Text vs crop" (the blind reader's codes and detail when a read exists); "Owner standard" (the fault list under the owner's standard, or "fine").
16:## 3. Frames: the two verdicts at a glance
18:- An **inner frame of the same thickness (3 px), inset 6 px**, is the **latest tool verdict**: green KEEP, red DROP, amber UNCERTAIN. Agreement reads as one colour, disagreement as two.
21:`↑` `↓` move between cards (also from inside the note box; focus follows). `SPACE` toggles the owner's mark KEEP ↔ DROP (first press KEEP; there is no empty state to cycle through); it also works inside an empty note box, and clicking the badge does the same. `z` zoom, `b` boxes, `d` details, `Esc` leaves the note box. A fixed tally top-right shows KEEP / DROP / unmarked.
23:**The card must fit the screen.** `↑` `↓` put the card's top at the top of the viewport, so the crop is seen first and the note box stays reachable. Every table cell is clamped to two lines; `d` (or a click on the table) opens the card's full text. Builders keep the version rows to a verdict and one clause and put long diagnostics after it, where the clamp hides them until asked. (Owner, 19 Oct: "there is like a huge body of text for every image and when I press down arrow I miss the top of the image or the notes box".)
25:**Never ask for a mark twice.** Lines the owner has already judged on an earlier sheet come LAST, carry `prior: KEEP|DROP` and show that mark as a dashed outer border (solid = marked on this sheet); the unjudged lines come first. The tally counts only this sheet's marks. (Owner, 19 Oct: "if they all have decisions why am I rejudging the changed ones?")
27:**Vertical segments get their own layout.** A crop taller than wide is placed on the left, displayed up to 640 px tall (3× cap still applies), with the text table, pills and note box on the right; horizontal crops keep the stacked layout. The builder adds the `tall` class and the JS also detects it from the overlay's viewBox for sheets built earlier. (Owner, 19 Oct: "on long vertical segments you can arrange them so that they are larger if they take up the left side of the box and the text takes the right".)
30:- Database collection `notes`, one document per card, id = `<sheet prefix>:<line_id>` (e.g. `segeval:gazette_modern--…-l0139`), fields `note`, `verdict` (`KEEP`|`DROP`|``), `printed` (correction sheets), `updated` (Europe/Athens, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM`), `line_id`.
37:| kind of tool | what the owner decides | mark | inner frame = tool state | rows that change |
39:| **Decision tools** (segmentation, admission, census verdicts) — the reference | keep or drop the line | KEEP / DROP | KEEP / DROP / UNCERTAIN | measurements + last two versions |
43:Rules for any variant: crop + text together; last two versions only; same frames, keys, autosave and republish protocol; the only free parameters are the row set, the overlay set and the meaning of KEEP/DROP, stated in the sheet's intro.
46:1. Cards from the tool's own evidence records (never re-run the tool in the builder); crop paths byte-exact to the record's hash.
50:5. Headless screenshot check; publish with `db`+`user`; stable ids; dump marks before any republish.
     8	
     9	`greekocr/harvest/line_pipeline.py` declares `PIPELINE_VERSION = "0.3.1"`. `docs/harvest/line_pipeline/tool_versions.json` supplies named tool generations and exact component hashes/digests. Versions count documented methods, not commits or measured accuracy.
