    21	| Composer | 0.2 | Compatible raw-parent spans, coverage and conflict checks |
    22	| Final eligibility | **0.3** | Cell exemption matches early gate; content/confidence/codec/CTC/split checks remain |
    23	| Census orchestration | **0.6** | Durable inventory, bounded parallel native execution, protected frozen-parent aliases and configured held-out crop union |
    24	| Codec | **v2** | `greekocr/_vendor/codec/v2.json`, NFD atoms; SHA256 `94485f72eac0aaf2324dc60b1c02110b271d362a79c440e2ce6bf6f4604997b9` |
    25	
    26	The superseded pipeline README and graph remain dated records under `docs/records/harvest/line_pipeline_legacy/`. The JS policy's historical “0.8” comment names the three-rule origin; current geometry and orchestration plus the adopted band make the complete tool **0.9-s5**.
    27	
    28	**Band adoption provenance:** this is a coordinator decision under the owner's end-to-end mandate (“you don't have to wait for me, resolve these end to end”), recorded in the coordinator ledger on **19 October at 21:34**. It was reported to the owner in writing: “frozen the configuration at 0.9-s4 measurement, gate 0.3, band 0.30–2.00, one band for everything”. The task records no objection since. This provenance is supplied by the coordinator; it is **not an owner ruling**. The one inclusive 0.30–2.00 band applies to numeric/non-numeric and small/non-small rows, with mode 2, padding 1.5, the gate and S4 measurement unchanged. It was fitted on owner marks; this adoption is not an independent generalization result.
    29	
    30	SEG10 ports the exact archived census03 hunks: `automatic_result()` uses `not re.search(r"\d\s*[.\-·]\s*\d", text)` for numeric candidate negatives, and `Ledger.deduplicate()` unions `final_policy.heldout_crop_sha256` into its existing held-out set. The deployed census04 package remains a separate historical 0.8 build; its results are not a current production census. Tool iterations move numerics 0.2→0.3 (the returned automatic result is bound to the numerics manifest entry) and census 0.5→0.6. Segmentation appends its thirteenth documented iteration, 0.9-s4→0.9-s5 (the existing suffix convention is eight base iterations plus five steps); pipeline 0.3→0.3.1 is a patch identifier. All other tool generation numbers remain unchanged; exact shared component hashes are regenerated.
    31	
    32	## Entry points and responsibility
    33	
    34	`greekocr.harvest.line_pipeline_census` is the top-level census CLI. `line_pipeline.py` evaluates one canonical row; `line_pipeline_sources.py` adapts existing parents; `line_pipeline_adapters.py` imports earlier SF7/RU1/N1 results; `line_pipeline_native.py` obtains native evidence; `line_pipeline_parallel.py` bounds worker concurrency; `line_pipeline_runtime.py` binds the actual runtime. The Rust service in `scripts/harvest/filter_runtime/` performs frozen predictor inference; it is not a new detector or fit.
